.TH SYSTEM-MONITOR-SWAY 1 "2026-09-19" "system-monitor-sway" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
system-monitor-sway \- stacked CPU/memory/network graphs for Sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B system-monitor-sway
[\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR] [\fB\-\-self\-check\fR] [\fB\-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GNOME system-monitor style stacked area charts for
.BR Sway "(Wayland)" ,
anchored to the center of the top bar via
.BR gtk-layer-shell
(over the Waybar strip).
GNOME is not required.
.PP
Graphs shown are configured in
.IR config.json ;
by default cpu, memory and net are displayed.
Optional graphs: freq, swap, disk, gpu, thermal, fan, battery.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fICONFIG\fR
Use
.I CONFIG
instead of the first config found.
.TP
.BR \-\-self\-check
Run lightweight sanity checks and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/system-monitor-sway/config.json
User config (first file that exists wins; see README for full order).
.TP
.I /etc/system-monitor-sway/config.json
System-wide config.
.TP
.I /usr/share/system-monitor-sway/config.json
.br
.I /usr/local/share/system-monitor-sway/config.json
Shipped default config.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base for the user config lookup.
.TP
.B GDK_BACKEND
Forced to
.I wayland
if unset; required for gtk-layer-shell under Sway.
.TP
.B SYSTEM_MONITOR_SWAY_DEBUG
If set, log layer-shell placement diagnostics to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Autostart in \fB~/.config/sway/config\fR (exec section):
.EX
exec waybar
exec /usr/bin/system-monitor-sway
.EE
.TP
Run once without relogin:
.EX
swaymsg exec /usr/bin/system-monitor-sway
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR swaymsg (1),
.BR waybar (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jerome Berclaz.
